pokeplatinum-hostlayout.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): pointers held in 32-bit integers,
found by tools/plat_lint.py (check C4; docs/platinum.md). On the DS an address fits a u32; on the host a pointer is 64
bits, so a value that is really a pointer must travel as uintptr_t. Two groups reached a u32:
 - the H-blank offset-register address of the screen scroll and shake effects: libntr's REG_BGxHOFS_ADDR is the
   address of a host variable, passed as `u32 bg` through ScreenScrollManager_ScrollX/Y, ScreenScrollTask_Scroll,
   ScreenShakeEffect_Start (the water encounter effect), ov104_0223F0B0/ov104_0223F1B4 (the Frontier scene effects) and
   CustomBgScrollContext_New/BattleAnimUtil_GetHOffsetRegisterForBg (battle backgrounds), into a u32 field that is cast
   back to `void *` for BufferManager_StartDMA: the DMA target was the low half of the address;
 - the Giratina/Shaymin icon refresh in the PC boxes: `u32 vramAddr` held G2_GetOBJCharPtr() plus an offset, then
   was copied to as a `void *`.
No struct that is read from a file changes; the structs touched are runtime state (ScreenScrollManager,
CustomBgScrollContext, UnkStruct_ov104_0223F174).

